                &lt;div&gt;
                    
                        &lt;article&gt;
                            &lt;h2&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/StackExchange/StackExchange.Redis/releases/tag/2.13.1"&gt;2.13.1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
                            &lt;div&gt;
                                &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;IMPORTANT:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt; This release changes the default protocol from RESP2 to RESP3 for Azure Managed Redis endpoints (only); this&lt;br&gt;
has scalability and feature advantages, but if you are using modules or ad-hoc commands, &lt;em&gt;&lt;a href="https://stackexchange.github.io/StackExchange.Redis/Resp3" rel="nofollow"&gt;please see the RESP3 notes&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;, which includes:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;the purpose of RESP3&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;scenarios where RESP2 vs RESP3 may be visible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;how to explicitly choose to remain on RESP2&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;notes on additional libraries such as NRedisStack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What's Changed&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prefer RESP3 for Azure Managed Redis endpoints (&lt;a href="https://github.com/StackExchange/StackExchange.Redis/pull/3067" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/StackExchange/StackExchange.Redis/pull/3067/hovercard"&gt;#3067 by @mgravell&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full Changelog&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;a class="commit-link" href="https://github.com/StackExchange/StackExchange.Redis/compare/2.12.27...2.13.1"&gt;&lt;tt&gt;2.12.27...2.13.1&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
                            &lt;/div&gt;
                        &lt;/article&gt;
                    
